{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3j4JCQGYAqsviNjiCur","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't changed anything for this one. Adding a per-day breakdown to `out/summary.csv` would break what the partner already gets from the portal.\n\n`scripts/summarize.py` says the portal only accepts `period,total,count`, one row per period, and **silently cuts off anything past 50 lines**. The 2025 data covers 248 distinct days. If I add those rows, the file goes from 12 lines to about 260. The partner would get the first ~49 rows and no error. If the daily rows are listed after the monthly ones, they'd keep the 11 months but get only about 38 days, all from early January. And nothing would show the data was incomplete.\n\nWays to give them per-day figures without that:\n\n1. **A separate file**, such as `out/summary_daily.csv`, built by the same script. `summary.csv` stays as it is. This only works if the partner can fetch a second file. If that file also goes through the portal, it would have the same 50-line limit.\n2. **Something that fits in 50 lines**, like per-weekday totals or the busiest days.\n3. **The portal's limit changes first**, which is on their end.\n\nMy suggestion is option 1, if they can fetch a second file. Do you know how the partner would pull it?","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":229,"cache_read_input_tokens":20134,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":229,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-43>","timestamp":"2026-11-14T23:57:09.069Z","request_id":"gen-1794700622-XXhPmCSXzZhtL8o1xdCN"}
